**Deviations and notes:**
- **Source scan:** the new source-scan test found one more revert regex, in `web/src/main.ts`. It now uses `isRevertSubject`.
- **Link order:** links keep the parser's pass order (PR URLs, issue URLs, close keywords, bare refs). The spec says "message order", and I left the existing order alone so graveyard output doesn't shift.
- **Failed lookups:** a 404 on a linked issue fails the whole commit and leaves no entry, as REQ-1 says. That commit is retried on every run.
- **Invalid output file:** the command exits 1 and refuses to overwrite an existing invalid obituary file.
- **Types location:** the fetcher types (`FetchOutcome`, `GitHubFetcher`) live in `github.ts`.
- **Obituary file parser:** `parseObituaryFile` in `src/core/obituary.ts` also validates existing files for the command. Task 10 can reuse it.
- **Untracked label file:** `research/labels/revivals-new-hand.jsonl` appeared at 15:50 during the session. I didn't create it, so I left it untracked and out of the commit.

